#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100609 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2f5234-df9c-5269-8702-30b4dde9a2ca" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by the Identity Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f7868f7f-b296-5a38-9af6-61dc4d1198a7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4408" :question/problem "Calculate the product $I_3 B$ given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100610 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column or Row of the Identity Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9832238f-baff-5527-a11a-c65b6529cb0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4410" :question/problem "Calculate the product $C D,$ if\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3,$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nDon't believe it? Let's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ -1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column or Row of the Identity Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9228cb9-585a-5f6f-bb50-d41711011f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279034} {:answer/id #uuid "c26801bd-4f21-5d47-b61b-29883a1f9efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279035} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e0c733-b35b-50ea-84d7-f989fd75cd74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279036} {:answer/id #uuid "534cefcc-eadd-5531-ad7f-ae5d9901da55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279037} {:answer/id #uuid "0be9da00-88e9-5d6d-9157-b1810eb736a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9228cb9-585a-5f6f-bb50-d41711011f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279034} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e9beb0-2e23-50ee-9d1b-bd0e3c85478b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d0b6a4e-efb1-5ae5-9574-5048a588b6e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130247" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ 0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2f5234-df9c-5269-8702-30b4dde9a2ca" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by the Identity Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49f73cee-b4a6-59b2-9533-74a783242bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279098} {:answer/id #uuid "acb56da7-c69a-5fc5-8ea7-e004233b23a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279099} {:answer/id #uuid "99d42236-dca2-531d-ba31-48e7b138dde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279100} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5c1c45-15ac-5eb6-871b-1828c386cb79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279101} {:answer/id #uuid "abeb432e-237f-5f51-887a-eee7ca8f11d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abeb432e-237f-5f51-887a-eee7ca8f11d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279102} :answer-field/id #uuid "3155ad0a-8145-538f-afcb-5578645ad5cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fd6de04-63a9-5f4e-b338-88b9712e3f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-75479" :question/problem "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{2}=Q=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
